From 7bbcb042a71b57dba286d33638848c188e5d4799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:31:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] :new: Add explicit cached producer memory ownership

Native CPU mappings need allocation identity, retained backing and explicit
noncoherent ownership before the real runtime can reuse their bytes.

Add an opt-in producer API with one runtime buffer per cached allocation,
whole-range physical alias resolution, retained CPU/native leases, and
flush/submit/wait/invalidate epochs. Refuse fragmented ranges, stale leases,
live exports and uncertain ownership. Expose additive C calls and statuses.
Keep the adopted resource Private and require the exact runtime device.

The owned-fixture runtime test, lease lifetime checks, seven ownership and
registry tests, two C export checks and scoped lint checks pass. The Pixel
root-shell diagnostic also passes through the unchanged strict QEMU native
worker and complete descendant reap before independent GPU readback.

The full workspace check remains blocked by unchanged formatting/lint
findings and unavailable CMake. This is an experimental interop API; it does
not wire general guest RAM, remaps or MMIO, or qualify app UID or iOS boot.
